.TH SWAYDESK-CLIPBOARD-POPUP 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.2.0" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-clipboard\-popup \- clipboard history popup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-clipboard\-popup
.SH DESCRIPTION
The cliphist history, with search in the full text, image thumbnails, pinned items kept apart from the history, and clearing the history. The keyboard stays in the search field: the arrows or Tab move the selection, and Enter copies the selected item. Waybar and Super+V open it.
.PP
Running it again while the popup is open closes it, and opening it closes the other popups of the bar. Esc, clicking outside or switching workspace also closes it.
.PP
The session runs it under the name waybar\-clipboard\-popup (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-clipboard\-popup); the process name is waybar\-clipboard\-popup too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/swaydesk/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language, accent color, GTK and icon themes, folder color, file manager, weather location and holidays.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cliphist (1),
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR swaydesk\-clip\-store (1),
.BR wl\-copy (1)
